diff --git a/HARMONY_RECOMP_NOTES.md b/HARMONY_RECOMP_NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..86b51b0499c8db2afa6a4005e354ad2afd814db7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/HARMONY_RECOMP_NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@
+# HarmonyRecomp Notes for ReXGlue Development
+
+Last updated: 2026-08-27
+
+HarmonyRecomp is a multi-image Xbox 360 static recompilation target consisting
+of `default.xex` plus six dynamically loaded player DLLs. Keep reusable ReXGlue
+fixes here separate from Harmony-specific function overrides.
+
+Hosted redistributable builds use `REXGLUE_USE_PREGENERATED=ON` to compile the
+project's committed generated sources without invoking codegen or requiring
+private guest binaries. The generated CMake integration makes the codegen
+target a no-op in that mode and rejects projects that do not provide generated
+entrypoint sources. Local regeneration keeps the default mode and still runs
+normal dependency-aware codegen.
+
+## Runtime-verified behavior
+
+- All six current modules—Alucard, Soma, Charlotte, Jonathan, Shanoa, and Axe
+  Armor—have completed at least one normal gameplay chapter.
+- Soma has also completed multi-chapter testing and real unload/reload cycles.
+- Shanoa's former `0x83269E18` failure was a discovery omission, not a module
+  lifecycle failure. It is now represented by a Harmony module override and is
+  manually retested through chapter completion.
+
+## Function discovery
+
+Valid executable targets referenced only through vtables, function-pointer
+tables, initializer arrays, or small tail-thunk families may be omitted.
+Harmony currently uses source-level per-image overrides after recovering exact
+PPC and function bounds. A general upstream improvement should discover and
+validate these data-referenced executable targets without treating arbitrary
+data as code.
+
+## Dispatch isolation and explicit table bases
+
+Each recompiled image must use one explicit `function_table_base` contract for
+both generated indirect lookup code and runtime table initialization.
+
+- Harmony default image: `0x88000000`
+- Player DLLs: their existing non-overlapping `image_base + image_size` bases
+
+Generated code uses `REX_FUNCTION_TABLE_BASE`; runtime initialization consumes
+the same generated module metadata. Do not restore an independent runtime-only
+Harmony conditional or recompute the base separately in the indirect-call
+template. The former contract mismatch produced a read at `0x833B0D00` for a
+valid target and is fixed.
+
+Repository state note: the explicit-base implementation, LAN session groundwork,
+socket/overlapped support, and focused tests were checkpointed in
+`d4a15c86f215ffff88f29bbbb69fa971f0f7b39e`. The separately dirty
+`thirdparty/libmspack` submodule and untracked `C:/` path are unrelated and
+should remain excluded from Harmony commits.
+
+## LAN multiplayer checkpoint
+
+ReXGlue now has configurable LAN identity, an opt-in online-capable profile,
+runtime-backed XSession records, UDP discovery/join/leave, basic XNet address
+and key mappings, explicit LAN bind/gameplay ports, and a polled Winsock
+overlapped receive path. Harmony can discover the other machine, form a
+two-member session, complete the gameplay handshake, and sustain bidirectional
+lobby traffic.
+
+The gameplay receive blocker is fixed by snapshotting the guest flags value at
+overlapped submission time; asynchronous completion no longer rereads a reused
+guest stack pointer. A later `XGISessionJoinRemote` failure was traced to an
+unbalanced object reference: `XamSessionRefObjByHandle` retained the pointer,
+while `ObDereferenceObject` released the handle. Retaining the handle instead
+prevents the session slot from being reused by the gameplay socket. Both fixes
+are paired-runtime verified through a successful join and sustained
+bidirectional UDP 30742 lobby traffic in DesktopHost log
+`harmonyrecomp_052.log` and Ally log `harmonyrecomp_055.log`.
+
+Focused receive-boundary diagnostics remain in `src/kernel/xam/xam_net.cpp`
+and `src/system/xsocket.cpp`. Search-result properties/contexts remain
+incomplete and may explain suspect lobby presentation, but are separate from
+the working transport and join path.
+
+The first internet-capable candidate adds an init-only
+`--direct_connect_address=<IPv4>` option. When empty, the existing limited-
+broadcast LAN search is unchanged. When set, XSession search sends the same
+discovery query by unicast through the configured local interface, keeps the
+manual endpoint authoritative across the advertisement and join response, and
+then reuses the existing XGI join, XNet mapping, and UDP gameplay path. UDP
+30741 remains the session query/join control port and UDP 30742 remains the
+translated gameplay port. Focused tests cover direct unicast discovery, full
+session identity preservation, membership join, and an advertised private
+address that differs from the explicit endpoint. Paired Tailscale runtime
+validation is still required; do not describe Direct Connect as runtime-
+verified until that succeeds.
+
+## Recompiled module lifecycle
+
+Commit `e8053e0` repairs the stale `module_libraries_` versus `user_modules_`
+lifecycle and dispatch isolation. Module identity is the stable registered guest
+path, not a later-mutated VFS/host path spelling. Duplicate requests for the same
+live guest module reuse the existing `UserModule`; unload removes all associated
+registries and its function mappings. Collision protection remains for genuinely
+different modules.
+
+The fix is runtime-verified: Soma completed two real unload/reload cycles without
+duplicate-load rejection, null guest reads, assertions, or fatal errors.
+
+## Input
+
+Commit `4909758` adds the MnK one-poll latch so short host keyboard presses are
+not lost between guest XInput polls. This is required for reliable keyboard
+START/menu input and is runtime-verified.
+
+## Harmony-specific constraints
+
+- Six guest modules occupy separate image and dispatch-table ranges; do not use
+  one global per-address mapping that lets default and DLL functions collide.
+- Full-game runtime testing uses `--license_mask=1` and Xenos.
+- Long interactive gameplay belongs to the user. ReXGlue changes should be
+  built and handed off with a focused test procedure.
+- Optional missing OPD sidecar probes are not evidence of a ReXGlue failure.
+- Do not solve Harmony discovery gaps with permanent generated-C++ edits; keep
+  them in Harmony override configuration until an upstream discovery solution
+  supersedes them with evidence.
